{
 "id": "veil-of-ignorance",
 "channel": "philosophy",
 "style": "clay",
 "title": "THE VEIL OF IGNORANCE",
 "angle": "If you didn't know who you'd be, would you really protect the unlucky, as Rawls said?",
 "logline": "Rawls lost two brothers to illnesses he caught first, so he asked what rules you'd pick without knowing your luck, and answered: protect the worst-off, but Harsanyi used the same veil to say raise the average, so researchers tested real people, who chose an average with a floor, but in a hospital the veil even pushed people to sacrifice the one.",
 "hook_text": "LUCK DECIDED WHO LIVED",
 "hooks": [
  "Only one group in eighty-one chose the rule this philosopher predicted.",
  "Design a society, but you don't know who you'll be in it."
 ],
 "world": {
  "scenery": "default"
 },
 "script": [
  {
   "text": "John Rawls's childhood illnesses killed two of his little brothers.",
   "beat": "hook"
  },
  {
   "text": "His diphtheria spread to Bobby; the next winter, his pneumonia spread to Tommy.",
   "beat": "hook",
   "link": "detail"
  },
  {
   "text": "So Rawls asked: what rules would you pick without knowing your luck?",
   "beat": "question",
   "link": "so"
  },
  {
   "text": "Rich or poor, healthy or sick, you might be anyone.",
   "beat": "question",
   "link": "detail"
  },
  {
   "text": "His answer, in 1971: make the worst-off life as good as possible.",
   "beat": "reveal1",
   "link": "answer",
   "say": "His answer, in nineteen seventy-one: make the worst-off life as good as possible."
  },
  {
   "text": "Because behind this veil of ignorance, the worst-off life might be yours.",
   "beat": "reveal1",
   "link": "because"
  },
  {
   "text": "So a fair society is judged by its bottom, not its average.",
   "beat": "reveal1",
   "link": "so"
  },
  {
   "text": "But economist John Harsanyi had used the same veil earlier.",
   "beat": "reveal2",
   "link": "but",
   "say": "But economist John Harshahnyi had used the same veil earlier."
  },
  {
   "text": "His answer was the opposite: raise the average, even if a few lose badly.",
   "beat": "reveal2",
   "link": "detail"
  },
  {
   "text": "So one blindfold gave two thinkers two different societies.",
   "beat": "reveal2",
   "link": "so"
  },
  {
   "text": "So researchers put real people behind the veil.",
   "beat": "reveal3",
   "link": "so"
  },
  {
   "text": "Eighty-one groups in America, Canada and Poland had to agree on one rule.",
   "beat": "reveal3",
   "link": "detail"
  },
  {
   "text": "Only one group chose Rawls's rule; only ten chose Harsanyi's.",
   "beat": "reveal3",
   "link": "detail",
   "say": "Only one group chose Rawls's rule; only ten chose Harshahnyi's."
  },
  {
   "text": "Most chose a mix: raise the average, but guarantee everyone a floor.",
   "beat": "reveal3",
   "link": "but"
  },
  {
   "text": "But in 2019, a Harvard team asked: take one patient off oxygen to save nine earthquake victims?",
   "beat": "turn",
   "link": "but",
   "say": "But in twenty nineteen, a Harvard team asked: take one patient off oxygen to save nine earthquake victims?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Imagining they could be any of the ten, more people chose the nine.",
   "beat": "turn",
   "link": "detail"
  },
  {
   "text": "So behind the veil, we protect a floor, then play the odds.",
   "beat": "payoff",
   "link": "answer"
  },
  {
   "text": "But if you could be anyone, would you unplug the one you might be?",
   "beat": "payoff",
   "link": "but"
  }
 ],
